5 Usage
*******

5.1 Automatic Link Creation
===========================

When ‘autoslip-roam-mode’ is enabled, creating a new note with a
folgezettel address automatically:

  1. Identifies the parent note based on the address
  2. Inserts a backlink under ‘** Parent Note’ in the new note
  3. Inserts a forward link under ‘** Child Notes’ in the parent

5.2 Creating Child Notes
========================

The recommended way to create child notes:

     M-x autoslip-roam-insert-next-child

   This command:
  1. Reads the current note's folgezettel address
  2. Suggests the next available child address
  3. Prompts for a title
  4. Creates the note with proper bidirectional links

5.3 Manual Link Addition
========================

For existing notes without links:

     M-x autoslip-roam-add-backlink-to-parent

   A link that is already there is left alone, so the command is safe to
run twice.  To repair the whole vault in one step, *note Repairing
Links::.

5.4 Creating Child Notes from Lisp
==================================

Other packages can create a child note without prompts:

     (autoslip-roam-create-child parent-node "Title" address immediate)

 -- Function: autoslip-roam-create-child parent-node title &optional
          address immediate templates
     Create a child note of PARENT-NODE with TITLE and link the two
     notes.  PARENT-NODE is an org-roam node whose title carries a
     folgezettel address.  When ADDRESS is nil, the next free address is
     used.  When IMMEDIATE is non-nil, the capture is finished without
     showing its buffer, the first template in TEMPLATES is used, and
     the new node is returned.  TEMPLATES defaults to
     ‘org-roam-capture-templates’.

     The function signals a ‘user-error’ when the parent has no address,
     when ADDRESS is not a valid child of the parent, or when ADDRESS is
     already in use.

   The companion package autoslip-noter uses this function to file
org-noter notes on PDF files in the zettelkasten.

5.5 Cross-Reference Links
=========================

When you insert a link to another org-roam note using ‘C-c C-l’ or
‘org-roam-node-insert’, a reciprocal link is automatically created in
the target note under ‘** Cross References’.

   This can be disabled:
     (setq autoslip-roam-auto-crosslink nil)


